WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.792
After Sima Yi died, his son Sima Zhao held the great power of Wei, and the young emperor was only his puppet.

00:00:10.142 --> 00:00:18.374
Sima Zhao was set on replacing Wei and becoming emperor himself; this ambition was so clear that even passersby on the road could see it.

00:00:18.724 --> 00:00:24.076
The common people whispered among themselves that everyone understood what was on his mind.

00:00:24.426 --> 00:00:32.658
The young emperor Cao Mao refused to be manipulated, and decided to personally lead the imperial guards in resistance against Sima Zhao.

00:00:33.008 --> 00:00:37.304
He led a small number of soldiers and bravely marched out of the palace.

00:00:37.654 --> 00:00:43.222
But Cao Mao had far too few people at his side, and his uprising failed very quickly.

00:00:43.572 --> 00:00:50.172
Cao Mao was killed by Sima Zhao's men at only twenty years old — a truly tragic end.

00:00:50.522 --> 00:00:55.394
When the news spread, everyone grieved for the young emperor.

00:00:55.744 --> 00:01:02.224
Later, Sima Zhao's son Sima Yan finally founded the Jin dynasty, fulfilling his father's ambition.

